# The Myriad Pools' trigger is above the spell it is about on the stack, and can resolve after that spell has gone: Bot2 counters
# the Faerie Miscreant in response (Counterspell, {U}{U}) once the trigger has Mox Ruby as its target. The spell is in the graveyard
# by then, so the ability uses what it last was on the stack (CR 608.2h, 707.2): Mox Ruby still becomes a copy of Faerie Miscreant
# until end of turn, a 1/1 flier, and reverts at the end of turn. The Faerie itself never enters, so it draws nothing (the hand stays at four cards).

